  "narration": {
    "title": "The Rookies Worth Watching in September",
    "intro": "The rookie class doesn't have a runaway star, but it has depth in both dugout corners. A Tigers bat leads the hitters, a pair of arms sit under a 2.30 ERA, and a Royals kid is quietly climbing. Here's the freshman board as the pennant races heat up.",
    "rookies_lead": "Eduardo Valencia paces the rookie hitters at a .924 OPS for Detroit, with Jonah Cox close behind at .883, but the power belongs to others: Esmerlyn Valdez has 16 homers for Pittsburgh and Munetaka Murakami leads the group with 29 for the White Sox. On the mound, Bradgley Rodriguez owns the shiniest line at a 1.99 ERA for San Diego, with Brandyn Garcia (2.20) and Didier Fuentes (2.27) right there.",
    "rookie_surge_lead": "Carter Jensen is the one on the move, nudging his OPS up 35 points to .759 in Kansas City. Not a leaderboard number yet, but the arrow points the right way for the young Royal."
  }
